% ================================================================ text helpers (ToUpper, "contains")

% "the upper case of ..." and "... contains ..." are answered by dfe_text.pl.

% ================================================================ funding elements (pages 37-38)

rule source_of_funding with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 37:
the source of funding of a learner is a source
    if the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning delivery has a FAM of type a type with code "107"
    and the upper case of the type is "SOF"
    and the source is "ESFA 16-19"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the source is "Other".

rule direct_funded with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 38:
a learning delivery is direct funded
    if the learning delivery has a FAM of type a type with code "320"
    and the upper case of the type is "LDM".

rule funding_line_type with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 37 and 38:
the funding line type of a learner is a funding line type
    if the source of funding of the learner is "ESFA 16-19"
    and the age at 31 August of the learner is an age
    and the age is in [14, 15]
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is direct funded
    and the funding line type is "14-16 Direct Funded Students"
    otherwise the source of funding of the learner is "ESFA 16-19"
    and the age at 31 August of the learner is a second age
    and the second age < 19
    and the HNS FAM code of the learner is 1
    and the funding line type is "16-19 High Needs Students"
    otherwise the source of funding of the learner is "ESFA 16-19"
    and the age at 31 August of the learner is a third age
    and the third age < 19
    and it is not the case that the HNS FAM code of the learner is 1
    and the funding line type is "16-19 Students (excluding High Needs Students)"
    otherwise the source of funding of the learner is "ESFA 16-19"
    and the age at 31 August of the learner is a fourth age
    and the fourth age >= 19
    and the fourth age <= 24
    and the learner is EHC
    and the funding line type is "19-24 Students with an EHCP"
    otherwise the source of funding of the learner is "ESFA 16-19"
    and the age at 31 August of the learner is a fifth age
    and the fifth age >= 19
    and the funding line type is "19+ Continuing Students (excluding EHCP)"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the funding line type is "Unknown".

rule base_programme_funding with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 38:
the base programme funding of a learner is an amount
    if the national rate of the learner is a NR
    and the provider's historic retention factor is a RF
    and the provider's historic programme weighting is a PW
    and the amount = NR * RF * PW.

rule on_programme_funding with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 38:
the on programme funding of a learner is an amount
    if the learner is a start
    and the funding line type of the learner is a funding line type
    and the funding line type is different from "14-16 Direct Funded Students"
    and the base programme funding of the learner is a BPF
    and the provider's historic disadvantage proportion is a DP
    and the provider's large programme proportion is a LP
    and the provider's historic English and maths proportion is a EM
    and the provider's historic 16 to 18 area cost factor is a AC
    and the amount = BPF * (1 + DP) * (1 + LP) * (1 + EM) * AC
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the amount = 0.

% ================================================================ condition of funding (pages 39-48)

rule grade_c_or_above_english with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 39:
a learner has grade C or above English
    if the GCSE English grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["A*", "A", "B", "C", "9", "8", "7", "6", "5", "4"].

rule grade_c_or_above_english_ecf with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 39:
a learner has grade C or above English
    if the GCSE English grade of the learner is a grade
    and the ECF FAM code of the learner is 3.

rule grade_c_or_above_maths with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 39:
a learner has grade C or above maths
    if the GCSE maths grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["A*", "A", "B", "C", "9", "8", "7", "6", "5", "4"].

rule grade_c_or_above_maths_mcf with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 39:
a learner has grade C or above maths
    if the GCSE maths grade of the learner is a grade
    and the MCF FAM code of the learner is 3.

rule kings_trust_team with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 40:
a learning delivery is King's Trust TEAM
    if the learning delivery is a core aim
    and the learning delivery has a FAM of type a type with code "331"
    and the upper case of the type is "LDM"
    and the learning aim reference of the learning delivery is a reference
    and the reference is in ["60023995", "60027307", "60027629", "60032121", "60032868", "60033344"]
    and the learning delivery has a LARS validity as a LARS validity
    and the category of the LARS validity is a category
    and the upper case of the category is "1619_EFA"
    and the validity start date of the LARS validity is a validity start
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is a start
    and the start is after or equal to the validity start
    and it is not the case that
        the last date for new starts of the LARS validity is a last date
        and the start is after the last date.

rule english_grade_d with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 40:
a learner has English GCSE grade D
    if the GCSE English grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["D", "3"].

rule maths_grade_d with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 40:
a learner has maths GCSE grade D
    if the GCSE maths grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["D", "3"].

rule english_below_grade_d with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 40:
a learner has English below GCSE grade D
    if the GCSE English grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["E", "F", "G", "U", "X", "NONE", "2", "1"].

rule maths_below_grade_d with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 41:
a learner has maths below GCSE grade D
    if the GCSE maths grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["E", "F", "G", "U", "X", "NONE", "2", "1"].

% The list of rate bands that the rules of pages 41-47 repeat, row by row.
rule tl_ft_4a_bands with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 41:
the rate band of a learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    if the rate band of the learner is a band
    and the band is in ["1730 hours (T level Band 9)", "1580 hours (T level Band 8 uplifted)", "1580 hours (T level Band 8)", "1380 hours (T level Band 7 uplifted)", "1380 hours (T level Band 7)", "1180 hours (T level Band 6 uplifted)", "1180 hours (T level Band 6)", "580 to 1179 hours (T level Band 5)", "580+ hours (Band 5)", "485+ hours (Band 4a)"].

rule english_cof_validity with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 41:
a learning delivery has a valid English condition of funding validity
    if the number of LARS validity records of the learning delivery is a N
    and N > 0
    and the learning delivery has a LARS validity as a LARS validity
    and the category of the LARS validity is a category
    and the upper case of the category is "EFACONFUNDENGLISH"
    and the validity start date of the LARS validity is a validity start
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is a start
    and the start is after or equal to the validity start
    and it is not the case that
        the last date for new starts of the LARS validity is a last date
        and the start is after the last date.

rule maths_cof_validity with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 43:
a learning delivery has a valid maths condition of funding validity
    if the number of LARS validity records of the learning delivery is a N
    and N > 0
    and the learning delivery has a LARS validity as a LARS validity
    and the category of the LARS validity is a category
    and the upper case of the category is "EFACONFUNDMATHS"
    and the validity start date of the LARS validity is a validity start
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is a start
    and the start is after or equal to the validity start
    and it is not the case that
        the last date for new starts of the LARS validity is a last date
        and the start is after the last date.

% Pages 41-43 write this rule as four groups. The first ("both") is read as
% joined to the others by "or", as in the maths rule of page 42.
rule recognised_english_ecf with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 41:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE English qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the ECF FAM code of the learner is 4.

rule recognised_english_validity with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 41:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE English qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a valid start for CoF
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has English GCSE grade D
        and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and the learning delivery has a valid English condition of funding validity.

rule recognised_english_grade_d with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 41 and 42:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE English qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a valid start for CoF
    and the learner has English GCSE grade D
    and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and the ESFA condition of funding type of the learning delivery is 1
    and the learning delivery has a valid English condition of funding validity.

rule recognised_english_team with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 42:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE English qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a valid start for CoF
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has English GCSE grade D
        and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and the learning delivery is King's Trust TEAM.

rule recognised_maths_mcf with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 42:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE maths qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the MCF FAM code of the learner is 4.

rule recognised_maths_validity with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 42 and 43:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE maths qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a valid start for CoF
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has maths GCSE grade D
        and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and the learning delivery has a valid maths condition of funding validity.

rule recognised_maths_grade_d with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 43:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE maths qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a valid start for CoF
    and the learner has maths GCSE grade D
    and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and the ESFA condition of funding type of the learning delivery is 1
    and the learning delivery has a valid maths condition of funding validity.

rule recognised_maths_team with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 43 and 44:
a learning delivery is a recognised GCSE maths qualification for a learner
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a valid start for CoF
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has maths GCSE grade D
        and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and the learning delivery is King's Trust TEAM.

rule english_exemption with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner is recognised as an English exemption
    if the ECF FAM code of the learner is a code
    and the code is in [1, 2].

rule maths_exemption with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner is recognised as a maths exemption
    if the MCF FAM code of the learner is a code
    and the code is in [1, 2].

rule fsl2_english with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner has Functional Skills Level 2 English
    if the ECF FAM code of the learner is 5.

rule fsl2_maths with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner has Functional Skills Level 2 maths
    if the MCF FAM code of the learner is 5.

rule cof_min_hours_english with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner has CoF minimum hours English
    if the EMH FAM code of the learner is 1.

rule cof_min_hours_maths with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner has CoF minimum hours maths
    if the MMH FAM code of the learner is 1.

rule cof_not_required_hours with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner is not required to meet the condition of funding
    if the total planned hours of the learner is a H
    and H <= 149.

rule cof_not_required_age with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner is not required to meet the condition of funding
    if the age at 31 August of the learner is an age
    and the age <= 15.

rule cof_not_required_t_level with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 44:
a learner is not required to meet the condition of funding
    if the latest programme of the learner is a T level
    and the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim start date of the learner is a start
    and the start is before 2022-08-01.

rule english_cof_status with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 45 and 46:
the English condition of funding status of a learner is a status
    if the learner is not required to meet the condition of funding
    and the status is "Condition of Funding Does Not Apply"
    otherwise the learner is recognised as an English exemption
    and the status is "Exempt from the GCSE English A*-C or 9 to 4 requirement"
    otherwise the learner has grade C or above English
    and the learner has a learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a recognised GCSE English qualification for the learner
    and the status is "Has English, Studying English"
    otherwise the learner has grade C or above English
    and the status is "Has English, Not Studying English"
    otherwise the learner has English GCSE grade D
    and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery
        and the second learning delivery is a recognised GCSE English qualification for the learner
        and the learner has CoF minimum hours English
    and the status is "Has English GCSE Grade D or Grade 3, Not studying GCSE English"
    otherwise the learner has English below GCSE grade D
    and the learner has Functional Skills Level 2 English
    and the status is "Has English below GCSE grade D or grade 3, holds English FSL2 pass"
    otherwise it is not the case that the learner has grade C or above English
    and the learner has a third learning delivery
    and the third learning delivery is a recognised GCSE English qualification for the learner
    and the learner has CoF minimum hours English
    and the status is "Doesn't have English, Studying English"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner has grade C or above English
    and the status is "Doesn't have English, Not Studying English"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the status is "".

rule maths_cof_status with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 47 and 48:
the maths condition of funding status of a learner is a status
    if the learner is not required to meet the condition of funding
    and the status is "Condition of Funding Does Not Apply"
    otherwise the learner is recognised as a maths exemption
    and the status is "Exempt from the GCSE Mathematics A*-C or 9 to 4 requirement"
    otherwise the learner has grade C or above maths
    and the learner has a learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a recognised GCSE maths qualification for the learner
    and the status is "Has Maths, Studying Maths"
    otherwise the learner has grade C or above maths
    and the status is "Has Maths, Not Studying Maths"
    otherwise the learner has maths GCSE grade D
    and the rate band of the learner is in the T level, full-time or band 4a bands
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery
        and the second learning delivery is a recognised GCSE maths qualification for the learner
        and the learner has CoF minimum hours maths
    and the status is "Has Maths GCSE Grade D or Grade 3, Not studying GCSE Maths"
    otherwise the learner has maths below GCSE grade D
    and the learner has Functional Skills Level 2 maths
    and the status is "Has Maths below GCSE grade D or grade 3, holds Maths FSL2 pass"
    otherwise it is not the case that the learner has grade C or above maths
    and the learner has a third learning delivery
    and the third learning delivery is a recognised GCSE maths qualification for the learner
    and the learner has CoF minimum hours maths
    and the status is "Doesn't have Maths, Studying Maths"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner has grade C or above maths
    and the status is "Doesn't have Maths, Not Studying Maths"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the status is "".

rule number_of_lars_validities with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 48:
the number of LARS validity records of a learning delivery is a number
    if a learner has the learning delivery
    and the number is the count of each LARS validity such that
        the learning delivery has the LARS validity as a LARS validity.

% ================================================================ national funding rate (pages 49-53)

% The rows are tried in the order the rule table prints them.
rule rate_band with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 50 and 51:
the rate band of a learner is a band
    if the learner is a T level student
    and the T level funding band of the learner is "9"
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H1
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 9" students is a T1 under table hours_thresholds
    and H1 >= T1
    and the band is "1730 hours (T level Band 9)"
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the T level funding band of the learner is "8 uplifted"
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H2
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 8 uplifted" students is a T2 under table hours_thresholds
    and H2 >= T2
    and the band is "1580 hours (T level Band 8 uplifted)"
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the T level funding band of the learner is a B3
    and B3 is in ["9", "8"]
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H3
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 8" students is a T3 under table hours_thresholds
    and H3 >= T3
    and the band is "1580 hours (T level Band 8)"
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the T level funding band of the learner is a B4
    and B4 is in ["8 uplifted", "7 uplifted"]
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H4
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 7 uplifted" students is a T4 under table hours_thresholds
    and H4 >= T4
    and the band is "1380 hours (T level Band 7 uplifted)"
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the T level funding band of the learner is a B5
    and B5 is in ["9", "8", "7"]
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H5
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 7" students is a T5 under table hours_thresholds
    and H5 >= T5
    and the band is "1380 hours (T level Band 7)"
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the T level funding band of the learner is a B6
    and B6 is in ["8 uplifted", "7 uplifted", "6 uplifted"]
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H6
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 6 uplifted" students is a T6 under table hours_thresholds
    and H6 >= T6
    and the band is "1180 hours (T level Band 6 uplifted)"
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the T level funding band of the learner is a B7
    and B7 is in ["9", "8", "7", "6"]
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H7
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 6" students is a T7 under table hours_thresholds
    and H7 >= T7
    and the band is "1180 hours (T level Band 6)"
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H8
    and the learning hours threshold for "T Level band 5" students is a T8 under table hours_thresholds
    and H8 >= T8
    and the band is "580 to 1179 hours (T level Band 5)"
    otherwise the total planned hours of the learner is a H9
    and the learning hours threshold for "full time" students is a T9 under table hours_thresholds
    and H9 >= T9
    and the learner is under 18 or HNS
    and it is not the case that the learner is a T level student
    and the band is "580+ hours (Band 5)"
    otherwise the total planned hours of the learner is a H10
    and the learning hours threshold for "part time band 4" students is a T10 under table hours_thresholds
    and H10 >= T10
    and the age at 31 August of the learner is a A10
    and A10 >= 18
    and it is not the case that the learner is HNS
    and it is not the case that the learner is a T level student
    and the band is "485+ hours (Band 4a)"
    otherwise the total planned hours of the learner is a H11
    and the learning hours threshold for "part time band 4" students is a T11 under table hours_thresholds
    and H11 >= T11
    and the band is "485 to 579 hours (Band 4b)"
    otherwise the total planned hours of the learner is a H12
    and the learning hours threshold for "part time band 3" students is a T12 under table hours_thresholds
    and H12 >= T12
    and the band is "385 to 484 hours (Band 3)"
    otherwise the total planned hours of the learner is a H13
    and the learning hours threshold for "part time band 2" students is a T13 under table hours_thresholds
    and H13 >= T13
    and the band is "300 to 384 hours (Band 2)"
    otherwise the total planned hours of the learner is a H14
    and the learning hours threshold for "part time band 1" students is a T14 under table hours_thresholds
    and H14 >= T14
    and the band is "Up to 299 hours (Band 1)"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the band is "None".

rule learner_is_hns with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 51:
a learner is HNS
    if the HNS FAM code of the learner is 1.

rule learner_is_ehc with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 51:
a learner is EHC
    if the EHC FAM code of the learner is 1.

% The "either" of the full-time row of page 51.
rule under_18_or_hns_age with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 51:
a learner is under 18 or HNS
    if the age at 31 August of the learner is an age
    and the age < 18.

rule under_18_or_hns_hns with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 51:
a learner is under 18 or HNS
    if the learner is HNS.

rule national_rate with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 52:
the national rate of a learner is an amount
    if the rate band of the learner is "1730 hours (T level Band 9)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 9" students is a R1 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R1 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "1580 hours (T level Band 8 uplifted)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 8 uplifted" students is a R2 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R2 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "1580 hours (T level Band 8)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 8" students is a R3 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R3 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "1380 hours (T level Band 7 uplifted)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 7 uplifted" students is a R4 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R4 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "1380 hours (T level Band 7)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 7" students is a R5 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R5 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "1180 hours (T level Band 6 uplifted)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 6 uplifted" students is a R6 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R6 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "1180 hours (T level Band 6)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 6" students is a R7 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R7 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "580 to 1179 hours (T level Band 5)"
    and the national rate for "T Level band 5" students is a R8 under table national_rates
    and the amount = R8 / 2
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "580+ hours (Band 5)"
    and the national rate for "full time" students is the amount under table national_rates
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is a band 4
    and the band 4 is in ["485+ hours (Band 4a)", "485 to 579 hours (Band 4b)"]
    and the national rate for "part time band 4" students is the amount under table national_rates
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "385 to 484 hours (Band 3)"
    and the national rate for "part time band 3" students is the amount under table national_rates
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "300 to 384 hours (Band 2)"
    and the national rate for "part time band 2" students is the amount under table national_rates
    otherwise the rate band of the learner is "Up to 299 hours (Band 1)"
    and the national rate for "part time band 1 per FTE" students is a R14 under table national_rates
    and the FTE of the learner is a F14
    and the amount = R14 * F14
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the amount = 0.

rule t_level_hours_amount with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 89:
the T level hours amount of a learning delivery is a number
    if the learning delivery has an hours record of type a type with code 2 and amount the number
    and the upper case of the type is "HRS".

rule total_planned_hours with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 53:
the total planned hours of a learner is a number
    if the latest programme of the learner is a T level
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    and the T level hours amount of the learning delivery is a known amount
    and it is not the case that the learner is a 2021-2022 year or earlier T level starter
    and the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim sequence number of the learner is a S1
    and the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    and the aim sequence number of the second learning delivery is S1
    and the T level hours amount of the second learning delivery is the number
    otherwise the latest programme of the learner is a T level
    and the learner has a third learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the third learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    and the T level hours amount of the third learning delivery is a second known amount
    and the learner is a 2021-2022 year or earlier T level starter
    and the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim sequence number of the learner is a S2
    and the learner has a fourth learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    and the aim sequence number of the fourth learning delivery is S2
    and the T level hours amount of the fourth learning delivery is a TH
    and the T level additional hours of the learner is a AH
    and the number = TH + AH
    otherwise the planned learning hours of the learner is a PLH
    and the planned employability, enrichment and pastoral hours of the learner is a EEP
    and the number = PLH + EEP
    otherwise the planned learning hours of the learner is the number
    otherwise the planned employability, enrichment and pastoral hours of the learner is the number
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule fte with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 53:
the FTE of a learner is a number
    if the total planned hours of the learner is a H
    and the funded hours per FTE is a FH
    and the number = H / FH.

% ================================================================ uplifts and factors (pages 54-63)

rule academic_flag with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 54:
the academic flag of a learning delivery is a flag
    if the learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    and the flag is false
    otherwise the learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim
    and the flag is false
    otherwise it is not the case that the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is a known type
    and the flag is false
    otherwise the learning delivery is general studies or critical thinking
    and the flag is false
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is a type 1
    and the type 1 is in ["0001", "0002"]
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is a type 2
    and the type 2 is in ["0003", "2999"]
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is "0016"
    and the upper case awarding organisation code of the learning delivery is "IB"
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is "1401"
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is "0016"
    and the learning aim reference of the learning delivery is a reference
    and the reference is in ["60147830", "60147829", "60148573", "60149450"]
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is a type 3
    and the type 3 is in ["1446", "1447"]
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is "1420"
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is a type 4
    and the type 4 is in ["1440", "1460"]
    and the flag is true
    otherwise the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is "1469"
    and the flag is true
    otherwise a learner has the learning delivery
    and the flag is false.

rule academic_aim with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 54:
a learning delivery is an academic aim
    if the academic flag of the learning delivery is true.

rule upper_awarding_organisation with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 54:
the upper case awarding organisation code of a learning delivery is a code
    if the awarding organisation code of the learning delivery is an original code
    and the upper case of the original code is the code.

rule general_studies with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 55:
a learning delivery is general studies or critical thinking
    if the learning aim reference title of the learning delivery is a title
    and the title contains "General Studies"
    and the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is a type
    and the type is in ["0001", "0002"].

rule critical_thinking with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 55:
a learning delivery is general studies or critical thinking
    if the learning aim reference title of the learning delivery is a title
    and the title contains "Critical Thinking"
    and the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is a type
    and the type is in ["0001", "0002"].

rule psychology with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 55:
a learning delivery is a psychology aim
    if the learning aim reference title of the learning delivery is a title
    and the title contains "Psychology".

rule psychology_lower with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 55:
a learning delivery is a psychology aim
    if the learning aim reference title of the learning delivery is a title
    and the title contains "psychology".

rule studying_academic with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 55:
a learner is studying an academic programme
    if the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning delivery is an academic aim.

rule new_retention_status with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 56 and 57:
the new retention status of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner is a start
    and the number = 0
    otherwise the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is an academic aim
    and the completion status of the learning delivery is a status
    and the status is in [1, 2, 6]
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the second learning delivery is an academic aim
    and the completion status of the second learning delivery is 3
    and the withdrawal reason of the second learning delivery is a reason
    and the reason is in [2, 7, 47]
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the learner has a third learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the third learning delivery is an academic aim
    and the completion status of the third learning delivery is 3
    and the withdrawal reason of the third learning delivery is a second reason
    and the planned duration of the third learning delivery is a PD3
    and PD3 >= 18
    and the learning start date of the third learning delivery is a start
    and the first day of the current funding year is a first day
    and the start is after or equal to the first day
    and the learning actual end date of the third learning delivery is an end
    and the two year programme first year end date is a year end
    and the end is after or equal to the year end
    and the number = 1
    otherwise it is not the case that the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a core sequence
    and the learner has a fourth learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the fourth learning delivery is the core sequence
    and the completion status of the fourth learning delivery is a second status
    and the second status is in [1, 2, 6]
    and the number = 1
    otherwise it is not the case that the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a second core sequence
    and the learner has a fifth learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the fifth learning delivery is the second core sequence
    and the completion status of the fifth learning delivery is 3
    and the withdrawal reason of the fifth learning delivery is a third reason
    and the third reason is in [2, 7, 47]
    and the number = 1
    otherwise it is not the case that the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a third core sequence
    and the learner has a sixth learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the sixth learning delivery is the third core sequence
    and the completion status of the sixth learning delivery is 3
    and the withdrawal reason of the sixth learning delivery is a fourth reason
    and the planned duration of the sixth learning delivery is a PD6
    and PD6 >= 18
    and the learning start date of the sixth learning delivery is a second start
    and the first day of the current funding year is a second first day
    and the second start is after or equal to the second first day
    and the learning actual end date of the sixth learning delivery is a second end
    and the two year programme first year end date is a second year end
    and the second end is after or equal to the second year end
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.5.

% MonthDifference(start, planned end): the number of whole months between them.
rule planned_duration with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 72:
the planned duration of a learning delivery is a number
    if the learning start date of the learning delivery is a start
    and the learning planned end date of the learning delivery is an end
    and the number of whole months from the start to the end is the number.

rule historic_retention with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 58:
the provider's historic retention factor is a number
    if the provider's retention factor is the number
    otherwise the number = 0.

rule new_programme_weighting_stage_1 with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 58:
the new programme weighting stage 1 of a learner is a number
    if the number of core aim records of the learner is a N
    and N > 0
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the programme weighting of the learning delivery is the number
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 1.

rule new_programme_weighting with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 59:
the new programme weighting of a learner is a number
    if the latest programme of the learner is a T level
    and the T level PCW of the learner is the number
    otherwise the latest programme of the learner is a transition programme
    and the national T level transition programme PCW of the learner is the number
    otherwise the new programme weighting stage 1 of the learner is 1
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is King's Trust TEAM
    and the number = 1.44
    otherwise the new programme weighting stage 1 of the learner is the number.

rule a_level_uplift with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 59:
a learning delivery is an A level aim attracting uplift
    if the learning delivery has a LARS category with reference 64
    and the funding model of the learning delivery is 25.

rule a_level_uplift_count with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 59:
the count of A level learning aims attracting uplift of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a learner
    and the number is the count of each learning delivery such that
        the learner has the learning delivery
        and the learning delivery is an A level aim attracting uplift.

rule low_pcw_academic with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 59:
a learner meets the low PCW criteria
    if the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the count of A level learning aims attracting uplift of the learner is a N
    and N > 1.

rule low_pcw_vocational with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 59:
a learner meets the low PCW criteria
    if the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a SSA
    and SSA is in [1.1, 1.2].

rule low_pcw_vocational_science with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 59:
a learner meets the low PCW criteria
    if the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner is studying an academic programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is 2.1
    and it is not the case that the learning delivery is a psychology aim.

rule learning_delivery_programme_weighting with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 60:
the programme weighting of a learning delivery is a number
    if a learner has the learning delivery
    and the learner meets the low PCW criteria
    and the number = 1.15
    otherwise a second learner has the learning delivery
    and the second learner is studying an academic programme
    and the number = 1
    otherwise a learner has the learning delivery
    and it is not the case that the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a known area
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a SSA1
    and SSA1 is in [3.1, 3.2, 3.3]
    and the count of postcode specialist resource records of the learning delivery is a C1
    and C1 > 0
    and the learning delivery has a specialist resource postcode
    and the number = 2.09
    otherwise the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a SSA2
    and SSA2 is in [3.1, 3.2, 3.3]
    and the count of postcode specialist resource records of the learning delivery is 0
    and the provider has specialist resources
    and the number = 2.09
    otherwise the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a SSA3
    and SSA3 is in [4.1, 4.2, 4.3, 5.2]
    and the number = 1.73
    otherwise the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a SSA4
    and SSA4 is in [3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4]
    and the number = 1.58
    otherwise the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a SSA5
    and SSA5 is in [7.4, 6.1]
    and the number = 1.44
    otherwise the sector subject area tier 2 of the learning delivery is a SSA6
    and SSA6 is in [5.1, 5.3, 7.1, 7.3, 9.1, 9.2, 13.1, 13.2]
    and the number = 1.29
    otherwise a third learner has the learning delivery
    and the number = 1.

rule historic_programme_weighting with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 61:
the provider's historic programme weighting is a number
    if the provider's programme weighting is the number
    otherwise the number = 0.

rule historic_area_cost with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 61:
the provider's historic 16 to 18 area cost factor is a number
    if the provider's 16 to 18 area cost factor is the number
    otherwise the number = 0.

rule large_programme_proportion with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 61:
the provider's large programme proportion is a number
    if the provider's historic large programme proportion is the number
    otherwise the number = 0.

% TemporalFromRange and ValueAt (page 81): the value of the record whose range,
% from its effective from date up to the day after its effective to date (the
% end not included), contains the first day of the year.
rule record_in_force with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 62:
a record is in force on the first day of the current funding year
    if the effective from date of the record is a from date
    and the first day of the current funding year is a first day
    and the first day is after or equal to the from date
    and it is not the case that
        the effective to date of the record is a to date
        and the first day is after the to date.

% Page 62 tests the reference data against its "applicable effective to
% date", the day after its effective to date, with "on or earlier than": a
% record whose effective to date is 31 July 2026 still applies on 1 August.
rule postcode_record_applies with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 62:
a record applies on the first day of the current funding year
    if the effective from date of the record is a from date
    and the first day of the current funding year is a first day
    and the first day is after or equal to the from date
    and it is not the case that
        the effective to date of the record is a to date
        and a day after is 1 days after the to date
        and the first day is after the day after.

rule postcode_record_for_delivery with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 62:
a record is a postcode specialist resource record for a learning delivery
    if the record is a postcode specialist resource record
    and the postcode of the record is a postcode
    and the delivery location postcode of the learning delivery is the postcode
    and the record applies on the first day of the current funding year.

% As printed, the count is of the records in force on the first day of the
% year, whatever their postcode (page 62).
rule postcode_record_count with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 62:
the count of postcode specialist resource records of a learning delivery is a number
    if a learner has the learning delivery
    and the number is the count of each record such that
        the record is a postcode specialist resource record
        and the record applies on the first day of the current funding year.

rule specialist_resource_postcode with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 60 and 62:
a learning delivery has a specialist resource postcode
    if a record is a postcode specialist resource record for the learning delivery
    and the specialist resources of the record is "Y".

rule latest_delivery_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 63:
the latest learning delivery start date of a learner is a date
    if the learner has a learning delivery
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date.

% ================================================================ disadvantage (pages 64-65)

rule block_1_uplift with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 64:
the new block 1 disadvantage uplift of a learner is a number
    if the postcode disadvantage uplift of the learner is the number
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 1.

rule no_english_by_year_11 with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 64:
a learner does not have grade C or above English by year 11
    if the EDF FAM code 1 of the learner is 2.

rule no_english_by_year_11_second with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 64:
a learner does not have grade C or above English by year 11
    if the EDF FAM code 2 of the learner is 2.

rule no_maths_by_year_11 with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 64:
a learner does not have grade C or above maths by year 11
    if the EDF FAM code 1 of the learner is 1.

rule no_maths_by_year_11_second with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 64:
a learner does not have grade C or above maths by year 11
    if the EDF FAM code 2 of the learner is 1.

rule block_2_elements with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 64:
the new block 2 disadvantage elements of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner does not have grade C or above English by year 11
    and it is not the case that the learner does not have grade C or above maths by year 11
    and the number = 0
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner does not have grade C or above English by year 11
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner does not have grade C or above maths by year 11
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 2.

rule historic_disadvantage with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 65:
the provider's historic disadvantage proportion is a number
    if the provider's disadvantage proportion is the number
    otherwise the number = 0.

% ================================================================ English and maths funding (pages 66-67)

rule english_d_or_below with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 66:
a learner has English GCSE grade D or below
    if the GCSE English grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["D", "E", "F", "G", "U", "X", "NONE", "3", "2", "1"]
    and it is not the case that
        the ECF FAM code of the learner is a code
        and the code is in [2, 3].

rule maths_d_or_below with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 66:
a learner has maths GCSE grade D or below
    if the GCSE maths grade of the learner is a grade
    and the upper case of the grade is an upper grade
    and the upper grade is in ["D", "E", "F", "G", "U", "X", "NONE", "3", "2", "1"]
    and it is not the case that
        the MCF FAM code of the learner is a code
        and the code is in [2, 3].

rule english_exempt_ld with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 66:
a learner is exempt from GCSE English condition of funding due to a learning difficulty or prior attainment
    if the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that
        the ECF FAM code of the learner is a code
        and it is not the case that the code is in [1, 4, 5].

rule maths_exempt_ld with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 67:
a learner is exempt from GCSE maths condition of funding due to a learning difficulty or prior attainment
    if the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that
        the MCF FAM code of the learner is a code
        and it is not the case that the code is in [1, 4, 5].

rule english_instance with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 67:
a learner has an English instance
    if the learner has English GCSE grade D or below
    and the learner is exempt from GCSE English condition of funding due to a learning difficulty or prior attainment
    and the English condition of funding status of the learner is a status
    and the upper case of the status is an upper status
    and the upper status is different from "HAS ENGLISH BELOW GCSE GRADE D OR GRADE 3, HOLDS ENGLISH FSL2 PASS"
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H
    and H >= 150.

rule maths_instance with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 67:
a learner has a maths instance
    if the learner has maths GCSE grade D or below
    and the learner is exempt from GCSE maths condition of funding due to a learning difficulty or prior attainment
    and the maths condition of funding status of the learner is a status
    and the upper case of the status is an upper status
    and the upper status is different from "HAS MATHS BELOW GCSE GRADE D OR GRADE 3, HOLDS MATHS FSL2 PASS"
    and the total planned hours of the learner is a H
    and H >= 150.

rule english_maths_instances with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 67:
the English and maths instances of a learner is a number
    if the learner has an English instance
    and the learner has a maths instance
    and the number = 2
    otherwise the learner has an English instance
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner has a maths instance
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule historic_english_maths with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 67:
the provider's historic English and maths proportion is a number
    if the provider's English and maths proportion is the number
    otherwise the number = 0.

% ================================================================ date rules (pages 69-72)

rule summer_school with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 69:
a learner is a summer school student
    if the age at 31 August of the learner is an age
    and the age <= 15
    and the start date of the learner is a date
    and the 1st June of the current funding year is a June date
    and the date is after or equal to the June date.

rule learner_is_a_start_t_level with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 69:
a learner is a start
    if the learner is a T level student
    and it is not the case that the learner is a summer school student
    and the funding line type of the learner is a funding line type
    and the funding line type is different from "Unknown"
    and the qualifying period in days of the learner is a QP
    and QP > 0
    and the actual number of days this funding year of the learner is a AD
    and AD >= QP
    and it is not the case that
        the learner is a year 3+ T level student
        and it is not the case that the learner is repeating up to one full final year of T level.

rule learner_is_a_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 69:
a learner is a start
    if the learner is a learner
    and it is not the case that the learner is a T level student
    and it is not the case that the learner is a summer school student
    and the funding line type of the learner is a funding line type
    and the funding line type is different from "Unknown"
    and the qualifying period in days of the learner is a QP
    and QP > 0
    and the actual number of days this funding year of the learner is a AD
    and AD >= QP.

rule qualifying_period with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 70:
the qualifying period in days of a learner is a number
    if the total planned hours of the learner is a H
    and the learning hours threshold for "part time band 4" students is a T under table hours_thresholds
    and H >= T
    and the planned number of days this funding year of the learner is a PD1
    and PD1 >= 14
    and the number = 42
    otherwise the planned number of days this funding year of the learner is a PD2
    and PD2 >= 168
    and the number = 42
    otherwise the planned number of days this funding year of the learner is a PD3
    and PD3 >= 14
    and the number = 14
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule planned_days with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 70:
the planned number of days this funding year of a learner is a number
    if the start date this year of the learner is a start
    and the planned end date this year of the learner is an end
    and the end is after or equal to the start
    and the end is a D days after the start
    and the number = D + 1
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule actual_days with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 70:
the actual number of days this funding year of a learner is a number
    if the start date this year of the learner is a start
    and the actual end date this year of the learner is an end
    and the end is after or equal to the start
    and the end is a D days after the start
    and the number = D + 1
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule learner_start_date with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 70:
the start date of a learner is a date
    if the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is before the date.

rule start_date_this_year_as_computed with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 71:
the start date this year of a learner is a date as computed
    if the actual end date of the learner is an end
    and the first day of the current funding year is a first day
    and the end is before the first day
    and the date = uncertain
    otherwise the start date of the learner is a start
    and the first day of the current funding year is a second first day
    and the start is before the second first day
    and the date = the second first day
    otherwise the start date of the learner is a second start
    and the last day of the current funding year is a last day
    and the second start is before or equal to the last day
    and the date = the second start.

rule start_date_this_year with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 71:
the start date this year of a learner is a date
    if the start date this year of the learner is the date as computed
    and the date is different from uncertain.

rule learner_planned_end_date with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 71:
the planned end date of a learner is a date
    if the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning planned end date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
        and the learning planned end date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date.

rule planned_end_date_this_year_as_computed with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 71:
the planned end date this year of a learner is a date as computed
    if the start date of the learner is a start
    and the last day of the current funding year is a last day
    and the start is after the last day
    and the date = uncertain
    otherwise the planned end date of the learner is an end
    and the last day of the current funding year is a second last day
    and the end is after the second last day
    and the date = the second last day
    otherwise the planned end date of the learner is a second end
    and the first day of the current funding year is a first day
    and the second end is after or equal to the first day
    and the date = the second end.

rule planned_end_date_this_year with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 71:
the planned end date this year of a learner is a date
    if the planned end date this year of the learner is the date as computed
    and the date is different from uncertain.

rule adjusted_actual_end_date with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 71:
the adjusted actual end date of a learning delivery is a date
    if the learning actual end date of the learning delivery is the date
    otherwise the learning planned end date of the learning delivery is the date.

rule learner_actual_end_date with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 71:
the actual end date of a learner is a date
    if the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the adjusted actual end date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
        and the adjusted actual end date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date.

rule actual_end_date_this_year_as_computed with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 72:
the actual end date this year of a learner is a date as computed
    if the start date of the learner is a start
    and the last day of the current funding year is a last day
    and the start is after the last day
    and the date = uncertain
    otherwise the actual end date of the learner is an end
    and the last day of the current funding year is a second last day
    and the end is after the second last day
    and the date = the second last day
    otherwise the actual end date of the learner is a second end
    and the first day of the current funding year is a first day
    and the second end is after or equal to the first day
    and the date = the second end.

rule actual_end_date_this_year with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 72:
the actual end date this year of a learner is a date
    if the actual end date this year of the learner is the date as computed
    and the date is different from uncertain.

rule payment_period with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 72:
the payment period of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a start
    and the start date this year of the learner is a start date
    and the month of the start date is a M1
    and M1 <= 7
    and the number = M1 + 5
    otherwise the learner is a start
    and the start date this year of the learner is a second start date
    and the month of the second start date is a M2
    and M2 >= 8
    and the number = M2 - 7
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule learner_age with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 72:
the age at 31 August of a learner is a number
    if the date of birth of the learner is a birth date
    and the age on 2026-08-31 of someone born on the birth date is the number.

% ================================================================ date rules for the condition of funding (pages 73-74)

rule delivery_is_a_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 73:
a learning delivery counts as a start
    if the aim qualifying period in days of the learning delivery is a QP
    and QP > 0
    and the actual number of days of the learning delivery is a AD
    and AD >= QP.

rule valid_start_for_cof with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 73:
a learning delivery is a valid start for CoF
    if the learning delivery counts as a start.

rule delivery_qualifying_period with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 73:
the aim qualifying period in days of a learning delivery is a number
    if the planned number of days of the learning delivery is a PD1
    and PD1 >= 168
    and the number = 42
    otherwise the planned number of days of the learning delivery is a PD2
    and PD2 >= 14
    and the number = 14
    otherwise a learner has the learning delivery
    and the number = 0.

rule delivery_planned_days with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 73:
the planned number of days of a learning delivery is a number
    if the learning start date of the learning delivery is a start
    and the aim planned end date this year of the learning delivery is an end
    and the end is after or equal to the start
    and the end is a D days after the start
    and the number = D + 1
    otherwise a learner has the learning delivery
    and the number = 0.

rule delivery_actual_days with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 73:
the actual number of days of a learning delivery is a number
    if the learning start date of the learning delivery is a start
    and the adjusted actual end date of the learning delivery is an end
    and the end is after or equal to the start
    and the end is a D days after the start
    and the number = D + 1
    otherwise a learner has the learning delivery
    and the number = 0.

rule delivery_planned_end_this_year_as_computed with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 74:
the aim planned end date this year of a learning delivery is a date as computed
    if the learning start date of the learning delivery is a start
    and the last day of the current funding year is a last day
    and the start is after the last day
    and the date = uncertain
    otherwise the learning planned end date of the learning delivery is an end
    and the last day of the current funding year is a second last day
    and the end is after the second last day
    and the date = the second last day
    otherwise the learning planned end date of the learning delivery is the date.

rule delivery_planned_end_this_year with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 74:
the aim planned end date this year of a learning delivery is a date
    if the aim planned end date this year of the learning delivery is the date as computed
    and the date is different from uncertain.

% ================================================================ ESFA 16-19 and core aim selection (pages 75-76)

rule core_aim with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 75:
a learning delivery is a core aim
    if the aim type of the learning delivery is 5.

rule learner_core_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 75:
a learner has a learning delivery as a core aim
    if the learner has the learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a core aim.

rule number_of_core_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 75:
the number of core aim records of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a learner
    and the number is the count of each learning delivery such that
        the learner has the learning delivery as a core aim.

rule latest_core_aim_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 75:
the latest core aim start date of a learner is a date
    if the learner has a learning delivery as a core aim
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as a core aim
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date.

rule latest_tq_core_aim_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 75:
the latest T level TQ core aim start date of a learner is a date
    if the learner is a T level student
    and the learner has a learning delivery as a core aim
    and the learning aim reference type of the learning delivery is "1468"
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as a core aim
        and the learning aim reference type of the second learning delivery is "1468"
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date.

rule latest_core_aim_sequence with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 76:
the latest core aim sequence number of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a T level student
    and the latest T level TQ core aim start date of the learner is a TQ date
    and the number is the max of each sequence such that
        the learner has a learning delivery as a core aim
        and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the TQ date
        and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    otherwise the latest core aim start date of the learner is a core date
    and the number is the max of each second sequence such that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as a core aim
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is the core date
        and the aim sequence number of the second learning delivery is the second sequence
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule esfa_learning_delivery with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 76:
a learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the funding model of the learning delivery is 25.

% ================================================================ T levels (pages 77-89)

rule latest_core_aim_is_t_level with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 77:
the latest core aim of a learner is a T level programme
    if the latest core aim start date of the learner is a date
    and the learner has a learning delivery as a core aim
    and the programme type of the learning delivery is 31
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date.

rule t_level_student with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 77:
a learner is a T level student
    if the latest core aim of the learner is a T level programme.

rule latest_programme_t_level with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 77:
the latest programme of a learner is a T level
    if the latest core aim of the learner is a T level programme.

rule t_level_programme_aim with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 77:
a learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    if the programme type of the learning delivery is 31
    and the aim type of the learning delivery is 1.

rule learner_t_level_programme_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 77:
a learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    and the learner is a T level student.

rule number_of_t_level_programme_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 77:
the number of ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim records of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a learner
    and the number is the count of each learning delivery such that
        the learner has the learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim.

rule latest_t_level_programme_aim_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 78:
the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim start date of a learner is a date
    if the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date.

rule latest_t_level_programme_aim_sequence with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 78:
the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim sequence number of a learner is a number
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim start date of the learner is a date
    and the number is the max of each sequence such that
        the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim
        and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
        and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule latest_programme_aim_sequence with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 78:
the latest programme aim sequence number of a learner is a number
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim sequence number of the learner is the number.

% "earlier than the date 1 year before the first day of the current funding year"
rule year_3_plus with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 79:
a learner is a year 3+ T level student
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim start date of the learner is a start
    and the start is before 2025-08-01
    and the learner is a T level student.

rule early_t_level_starter with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 79:
a learner is a 2021-2022 year or earlier T level starter
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim start date of the learner is a start
    and the start is before or equal to 2022-07-31
    and the learner is a T level student.

rule transition_programme_aim with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 79:
a learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim
    if the programme type of the learning delivery is 30
    and the aim type of the learning delivery is 1.

rule learner_transition_programme_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 79:
a learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim
    if the learner has the learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim.

rule number_of_transition_programme_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 79:
the number of ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim records of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a learner
    and the number is the count of each learning delivery such that
        the learner has the learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim.

rule latest_transition_aim_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 80:
the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim start date of a learner is a date
    if the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date.

rule latest_transition_aim_sequence with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 80:
the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim sequence number of a learner is a number
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim start date of the learner is a date
    and the number is the max of each sequence such that
        the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 T level transition programme aim
        and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date
        and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule latest_programme_transition with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 80:
the latest programme of a learner is a transition programme
    if the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the programme type of the learning delivery is 30.

rule transition_student with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 80:
a learner is a transition student
    if the latest programme of the learner is a transition programme.

rule applicable_t_level_funding_band with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 81:
the applicable T level funding band of a learning delivery is a band
    if the learning delivery has a funding record as a LARS programme funding record
    and the funding record is in force on the first day of the current funding year
    and the funding band of the funding record is the band.

rule t_level_funding_band_stage_1 with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 81:
the T level funding band stage 1 of a learner is a band
    if the latest T level OS aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the applicable T level funding band of the learning delivery is the band.

rule t_level_funding_band with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 81:
the T level funding band of a learner is a band
    if the T level funding band stage 1 of the learner is the band
    and the band is in ["9", "8", "7", "6", "5", "8 uplifted", "7 uplifted", "6 uplifted"]
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the band is "5"
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the band is "0".

rule applicable_t_level_pcw with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 81:
the applicable T level PCW of a learning delivery is a number
    if the learning delivery has a funding record as a LARS programme funding record
    and the funding record is in force on the first day of the current funding year
    and the PCW of the funding record is the number.

rule t_level_pcw_stage_1 with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 82:
the T level PCW stage 1 of a learner is a number
    if the latest T level OS aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the applicable T level PCW of the learning delivery is the number.

rule t_level_pcw with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 82:
the T level PCW of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a T level student
    and the latest T level OS aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning aim reference of the learning delivery is a reference
    and the count of postcode specialist resource records of the learning delivery is a C1
    and C1 > 0
    and the learning delivery has a specialist resource postcode
    and the learning delivery has a funding record as a LARS programme funding record
    and the programme code of the funding record is a code
    and the code is in [52, 56]
    and the number = 2.09
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the provider has specialist resources
    and the latest T level OS aim sequence number of the learner is a second sequence
    and the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the second learning delivery is the second sequence
    and the learning aim reference of the second learning delivery is a second reference
    and the count of postcode specialist resource records of the second learning delivery is 0
    and the second learning delivery has a second funding record as a LARS programme funding record
    and the programme code of the second funding record is a second code
    and the second code is in [52, 56]
    and the number = 2.09
    otherwise the T level PCW stage 1 of the learner is a PCW
    and PCW > 0
    and the number = PCW
    otherwise the learner is a T level student
    and the number = 1
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule t_level_additional_hours with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 83:
the T level additional hours of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a 2021-2022 year or earlier T level starter
    and the number = 40
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule repeating_final_year with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 83:
a learner is repeating up to one full final year of T level
    if the learner is a T level student
    and the NLM FAM code 1 of the learner is 22.

rule repeating_final_year_second with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 83:
a learner is repeating up to one full final year of T level
    if the learner is a T level student
    and the NLM FAM code 2 of the learner is 22.

% The ZTPR0012 row of page 86 prints its last condition outside the "for at
% least one" above it; it is read here as inside, like the rows before it.
rule national_transition_pcw with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at pages 84 to 86:
the national T level transition programme PCW of a learner is a number
    if the latest programme of the learner is a transition programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning aim reference of the learning delivery is "ZTPR0001"
    and the count of postcode specialist resource records of the learning delivery is a C1
    and C1 > 0
    and the learning delivery has a specialist resource postcode
    and the number = 2.09
    otherwise the latest programme of the learner is a transition programme
    and the provider has specialist resources
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a second sequence
    and the learner has a second learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the second learning delivery is the second sequence
    and the learning aim reference of the second learning delivery is "ZTPR0001"
    and the count of postcode specialist resource records of the second learning delivery is 0
    and the number = 2.09
    otherwise the latest programme of the learner is a transition programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a third sequence
    and the learner has a third learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the third learning delivery is the third sequence
    and the learning aim reference of the third learning delivery is a reference
    and the national PCW for the reference is the number under table national_pcw
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 1.

rule t_level_os_aim with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 87:
a learning delivery is a T level OS aim
    if the programme type of the learning delivery is 31
    and the learning aim reference of the learning delivery is a reference
    and the reference contains "ZTLOS".

rule learner_t_level_os_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 87:
a learner has a learning delivery as a T level OS aim
    if the learner has the learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the learning delivery is a T level OS aim
    and the learner is a T level student.

rule learner_continuing_os_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 87:
a learner has a learning delivery as a continuing T level OS aim
    if the learner has the learning delivery as a T level OS aim
    and the completion status of the learning delivery is 1.

rule number_of_os_aims with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 87:
the number of T level OS aim records of a learner is a number
    if the learner is a learner
    and the number is the count of each learning delivery such that
        the learner has the learning delivery as a T level OS aim.

rule continuing_os_aim with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 88:
a learner has a continuing T level OS aim
    if the learner has a learning delivery as a continuing T level OS aim.

rule latest_os_aim_sequence with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 88:
the latest T level OS aim sequence number of a learner is a number
    if the learner has a learning delivery as a continuing T level OS aim
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is a date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a second learning delivery as a continuing T level OS aim
        and the learning start date of the second learning delivery is a second date
        and the second date is after the date
    and the number is the max of each sequence such that
        the learner has a third learning delivery as a continuing T level OS aim
        and the learning start date of the third learning delivery is the date
        and the aim sequence number of the third learning delivery is the sequence
    otherwise the learner has a fourth learning delivery as a T level OS aim
    and the learning start date of the fourth learning delivery is a third date
    and it is not the case that
        the learner has a fifth learning delivery as a T level OS aim
        and the learning start date of the fifth learning delivery is a fourth date
        and the fourth date is after the third date
    and the number is the max of each second sequence such that
        the learner has a sixth learning delivery as a T level OS aim
        and the learning start date of the sixth learning delivery is the third date
        and the aim sequence number of the sixth learning delivery is the second sequence
    otherwise the learner is a learner
    and the number = 0.

rule latest_tq_reference with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 88:
the learning aim reference of the latest T level TQ of a learner is a reference
    if the latest core aim of the learner is a T level programme
    and the latest core aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning aim reference of the learning delivery is the reference.

rule latest_os_reference with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 89:
the learning aim reference of the latest T level OS of a learner is a reference
    if the latest T level OS aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning aim reference of the learning delivery is the reference.

rule latest_t_level_actual_end with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 89:
the latest T level programme aim actual end date of a learner is a date
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning actual end date of the learning delivery is the date.

rule latest_t_level_planned_end with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 89:
the latest T level programme aim planned end date of a learner is a date
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning planned end date of the learning delivery is the date.

rule latest_t_level_start with provenance DfE 16 to 19 funding calculation 2026 to 2027 at page 89:
the latest T level programme aim start date of a learner is a date
    if the latest ESFA 16 to 19 T level programme aim sequence number of the learner is a sequence
    and the learner has a learning delivery as an ESFA 16 to 19 learning delivery
    and the aim sequence number of the learning delivery is the sequence
    and the learning start date of the learning delivery is the date.

